[list]
[*]Fixed: a colonist changed at a stand walked off and put on a duplicate of the clothing that stand was holding for them. A stand keeps a colonist's own kit while they are in uniform, and hides it from anything that goes looking for clothes, so a hauler cannot carry it off mid-shift. Mods that fetch clothing for a colonist read that hidden slot as an empty one and sent them to storage for a replacement, which came straight back off again when they changed out. Power armour made it obvious, since the colonist paid its equip time twice and finished where they started. A colonist is no longer sent after a garment their own stand is already holding. If that parked garment is worn through, they still go and find a better one. Nothing changes without a mod that dresses colonists for you.
[/list]
